    "Import failure, 8-second deadline, and oversized output rejected; following clean patch passed each time.",
    "Module mutation then a clean child asserting absence passed.",
    "Six helper unit tests passed: target module/thread rejection, clean parent, malformed/duplicate/nonstandard JSON rejection, combined size limit, report preservation."
  ],
  "unit_test_command": "python3 -m unittest discover -s rwx-blast-radius/tools -p test_experiment_guard_pool.py",
  "limits": [
    "Single native thread is necessary but does not prove inherited native locks, atfork callbacks, or dependency initialization fork-safe. Pin and audit dependency whitelist before production.",
    "Preloading third-party dependencies changes import ordering; only SQLGlot/tests cleanliness and tested outcomes have been established.",
    "Linux-only prototype relies on /proc/self/task, fork, process groups and rusage. No persistent mutated worker reuse.",
    "RLIMIT_FSIZE caps each output file at 2MiB; combined stdout/stderr over 2MiB rejects. Prototype is not an adversarial sandbox.",
    "Guard success proves imports/collection only, not patch harmlessness or completeness of dependency narrowing.",
    "No automatic replacement/fallback integration, cumulative production budget, or cross-platform support implemented.",
    "Performance timings vary under emulation and host load; compare sequential pairs, not first overlapping pilot.",
    "Sequential baseline benchmark preceded file-output cap/parser hardening; actual-patch and adversarial benchmark used output cap. Helper parser hardening subsequently passed six unit tests."
  ],
